AmyJune works with the Linux Foundation as a Certification Community Architect, supporting the Global Skills team in developing and maintaining certification exams and related documentation across the Foundation’s portfolio.

She is also a DrupalCamp organizer for Florida DrupalCamp, Drupal Camp Asheville, and DrupalCamp Colorado, a member of the Drupal Community Working Group’s Conflict Resolution Team, and a board member of the Colorado Drupal Association.

Her ongoing work as a hospice nurse keeps her connected to the real-world challenges many end users face. As part of her continued accessibility advocacy, she co-organizes A11yTalks, an online meetup focused on accessibility as a core part of building a more inclusive web.

AmyJune is passionate about helping people discover the many ways they can contribute to and belong in open source communities, well beyond writing code.

She is also known for her superpower: making any meeting 20% more awkward just by showing up.

You can see all of her past talks on her [speaking page](https://gitlab.com/volkswagenchick/AmyJuneH/-/blob/master/Presentations.md).
